# Andela Agentic Observability Platform — Project Map

> **Note**: As soon as the first feature lands, update each section with the actual file paths and 1-line responsibilities. Treat unfilled entries as TODOs to be replaced — not aspirational architecture.

## Top-level (from Req. doc Section 13)

```
Andela-task/
├── .cursor/                  # Cursor rules, skills, agents, mcp.json
├── AGENTS.md                 # short project overview for human + agent readers
├── README.md                 # public-facing setup, run, test instructions
├── prompts.md                # complete history of LLM prompts (assessment requirement)
├── docker-compose.yml        # backend + frontend + SQLite volume
├── tasks/                    # todo, lessons, manual test scenarios
├── docs/                     # design notes, ADRs
├── deck/                     # presentation slides
├── backend/                  # FastAPI backend (Python)
├── frontend/                 # React + Vite UI
├── sdk/                      # watchdog_client Python SDK
├── tests/                    # backend + AI evaluation tests
├── infra/                    # Dockerfiles, GitHub Actions, deployment
├── data/
│   └── runbooks/             # operational runbooks (RAG source)
├── scripts/                  # synthetic traffic generator, dev helpers
├── pyproject.toml            # Python project metadata + deps
└── .gitignore
```

## Backend (`backend/app/`)

| Path | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `app/main.py` | FastAPI app factory; router includes; exception handlers; lifespan (DB init, runbook loader) |
| `app/core/config.py` | `Settings` via `pydantic-settings`; env-driven GEMINI_API_KEY, DB URL, thresholds |
| `app/core/exceptions.py` | `DomainError` and subclasses |
| `app/db/base.py` | `Base = DeclarativeBase` |
| `app/db/session.py` | engine, `SessionLocal`, `get_db()` dependency |
| `app/db/init_db.py` | `Base.metadata.create_all` on startup |
| `app/models/event.py` | Event ORM model |
| `app/models/anomaly.py` | Anomaly ORM model |
| `app/models/incident.py` | Incident ORM model with status/severity enums |
| `app/models/alert.py` | Alert ORM model |
| `app/models/runbook.py` | Runbook + embedding ORM model |
| `app/models/metric_rollup.py` | Pre-aggregated rates per minute |
| `app/models/service_topology.py` | Service dependency graph |
| `app/models/llm_evaluation.py` | Persisted prompts + responses + metrics |
| `app/schemas/` | Pydantic v2 request/response models |
| `app/repositories/` | Data access — one file per aggregate |
| `app/ingestion/` | Log ingestion + normalization |
| `app/detection/strategies/` | Z-Score, EWMA, signature frequency, severity drift |
| `app/correlation/` | Event correlation engine |
| `app/topology/` | Service graph + blast radius |
| `app/incidents/` | Incident lifecycle service |
| `app/triage/agents/` | Classification, root cause, remediation, executive summary |
| `app/triage/llm_client.py` | `LLMClient` protocol + Gemini (google-genai) implementation |
| `app/triage/prompts.py` | Versioned prompt templates |
| `app/triage/prompt_log.py` | Persists every prompt to `llm_evaluations` and appends to `prompts.md` |
| `app/rag/` | Runbook loader, embedder, retriever |
| `app/alerts/channels/` | Dashboard, webhook, email_sim, slack_sim |
| `app/risk/risk_score_service.py` | Risk score calculation |
| `app/api/routes/` | Thin HTTP handlers |

## Frontend (`frontend/`)

Stack: React + Vite + TypeScript (strict) + Recharts. UI inspection done via the Browser MCP.

| Path | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `frontend/index.html`, `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json` | Vite config |
| `frontend/src/main.tsx` | React entry, Router, QueryClient |
| `frontend/src/App.tsx` | Layout + routes |
| `frontend/src/pages/OverviewPage.tsx` | Risk score, active incidents, alerts, services |
| `frontend/src/pages/IncidentCenterPage.tsx` | Incident list with severity, status, root cause |
| `frontend/src/pages/TopologyPage.tsx` | Service graph, dependency tree, blast radius |
| `frontend/src/pages/TrendsPage.tsx` | Error rate trend, incident timeline, severity, health |
| `frontend/src/pages/AIAnalysisPage.tsx` | Classification, root cause, remediation, executive summary, runbook references |
| `frontend/src/components/` | Domain components organized by page |
| `frontend/src/api/` | Typed fetchers (one file per resource) |
| `frontend/src/hooks/` | Shared hooks |
| `frontend/src/lib/` | Pure helpers |
| `frontend/src/test/` | Vitest setup |

## SDK (`sdk/watchdog_client/`)

| Path | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `sdk/watchdog_client/__init__.py` | Public API: `create_event`, `create_batch`, `get_incidents`, `get_alerts`, `get_risk_score`, `get_health` |
| `sdk/watchdog_client/client.py` | HTTP client with typed methods |
| `sdk/watchdog_client/models.py` | Pydantic models mirroring API contracts |
| `sdk/watchdog_client/exceptions.py` | SDK-level exceptions |
| `sdk/pyproject.toml` | SDK package metadata, semantic version |
| `sdk/README.md` | SDK usage examples |
| `sdk/tests/` | SDK tests |

## Tests (`tests/`)

| Path | Covers |
|------|--------|
| `tests/conftest.py` | engine, db, client, fake LLM fixtures |
| `tests/unit/test_event_normalization.py` | normalization signatures |
| `tests/unit/test_detection_*.py` | each detection strategy |
| `tests/unit/test_correlation_engine.py` | correlation grouping |
| `tests/unit/test_risk_score.py` | risk score formula |
| `tests/unit/test_topology.py` | blast radius |
| `tests/unit/test_triage_*.py` | each agent + executive summary |
| `tests/integration/test_events_api.py` | HTTP layer for events |
| `tests/integration/test_incidents_api.py` | HTTP layer for incidents |
| `tests/integration/test_pipeline_end_to_end.py` | ingestion → detection → incident |
| `tests/ai_eval/` | classification / root-cause / remediation accuracy |

## Scripts (`scripts/`)

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `scripts/synth_traffic.py` | Generate the 7 demo scenarios (normal, DB outage, auth failures, throttling, memory leak, dependency failure, Black Friday) |
| `scripts/seed_runbooks.py` | Load runbooks into the embedding store |

## Infra (`infra/`)

| Path | Responsibility |
